course: dictionary
lesson: 13776
title: Words that make you feel small
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intimidate means to frighten someone, or to make them feel nervous and less confident. Sometimes a bully does it on purpose, to make someone do what they want. Sometimes something big or new just makes you feel small, even if nobody means it to.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The bully stood very close, stared hard and said, "Give me your money," to intimidate the boy.» The threat and the staring tell you that intimidate means to scare someone into doing what you want.
explain: Intimidate can also describe how something feels. «The maths test looked intimidating at first.» Nobody is threatening you here, but the test makes you feel nervous. Ask yourself: am I being threatened, or do I just feel small and unsure?
fact: Intimidate means to frighten or threaten someone, often to make them do what you want.
fact: Intimidate can also mean to make someone feel nervous or less confident, even without meaning to.
fact: «Intimidated» means feeling nervous or scared of something, and «intimidating» means something that makes you feel that way.
fact: Bullies may intimidate people with threats, hard staring, crowding round someone, or nasty messages online.
fact: Clues that help: a threat, a frightened person, or a word like «scared» or «nervous» nearby usually means the word is about intimidation.
exercise: «The bully tried to intimidate Sam into giving him his lunch money.» What does intimidate mean here? | To make someone laugh | *To frighten or threaten someone to make them do what you want | To help someone carry a heavy bag | To give someone a present
exercise: «The maths test looked intimidating, but Maya read each question slowly.» What does intimidating mean? | Hard to see in the dark | Very easy and fun | *Making you feel nervous or less confident | Very quiet and calm
exercise: «The big dog made Tom feel intimidated.» Find and copy one word that is a form of intimidate. | big | feel | dog | *intimidated
test:
«Leo felt intimidated by the loud crowd.» What does intimidated mean? | *Nervous and less confident | Very hungry | Happy and relaxed | Cold and wet
«The players shouted loudly to intimidate the other team.» What does intimidate mean here? | To scare or pressure the other team | *To scare or pressure the other team, not to cheer them on | To cheer the other team on | To join the other team
exam:
Which sentence shows someone trying to intimidate another person? | Anna shared her crayons with her friend. | *The bully stood very close and stared, so the smaller boy would hand over his bag. | Dad made a cup of tea for everyone. | The sun came out after the rain.
